      "message": "In order to make the simulation as accurate as possible, the failJob method ultimately causes the fake executor to actually check the contents of the git repo on disk in order to decide if the job should fail when presented with the git repo contents of the change that should cause it to fail.  In other words, failJob means \"fail this job if you see the contents of this change\".  Very useful for testing a gating system.",
